Apple's 20th-anniversary iPhone lineup could feature slightly larger displays than the iPhone 18 Pro models, if a new leak shared on Weibo is accurate.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Mostly-Screen-iPhone-Purple-Feature-2027.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1033225" /><br/>
Prolific Chinese leaker <a href="https://weibo.com/6048569942/Rj6MNs5hS">Digital Chat Station</a> claims that early iPhone 20 Pro display specifications include a 6.41-inch screen with a resolution of approximately 2,686 × 1,236 pixels, while the iPhone 20 Pro Max is said to have a 6.96-inch display with a resolution of around 2,912 × 1,340 pixels.<br/>
<br/>
For comparison, the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max feature 6.27 inches (rounded to 6.3 inches) and 6.86 inches (rounded to 6.9 inches) respectively. Those figures are measured as a standard rectangle, while the actual viewable area is smaller because of the devices' rounded corners. Meanwhile, the iPhone 18 Pro and 18 Pro Max resolutions are 2,622 × 1,206 pixels and 2,868 × 1,320 pixels, respectively.<br/>
<br/>
The resolution increases track quite closely with the rumored increases in physical display size, suggesting Apple likely plans to keep roughly the same 460 ppi pixel density as the iPhone 18 Pro models. Digital Chat Station previously suggested the 6.96-inch display on the iPhone 20 Pro Max would likely be <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/21/iphone-20-pro-max-7-inch-display/">marketed as a 7-inch panel</a> if it reaches production.<br/>
<br/>
Apple last increased the size of its premium iPhone displays with the iPhone 16 Pro lineup in 2024. The iPhone 16 Pro grew from 6.1 to 6.3 inches, while the iPhone 16 Pro Max increased from 6.7 to 6.9 inches, thanks to slimmer bezels and slightly larger chassis dimensions. The leaked dimensions for the iPhone 20 Pro models suggest only a modest increase in overall screen size, but there could be a good reason for this. <br/>
<br/>
Echoing previous claims, the leaker says Apple is testing a "borderless quad-curved" display design, with the screen curving away on all four sides. We've already seen <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/24/20th-anniversary-iphone-micro-curved-oled-panel/">multiple</a> reports indicating that Apple's 20th-anniversary iPhone could resemble a single, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/04/28/20th-anniversary-iphone-liquid-glass-display/">uninterrupted slab of glass</a> where the metal frame bezels are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/08/25/what-20th-anniversary-iphone-may-look-like/">largely hidden</a> during normal use. <em>Bloomberg</em> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/16/20th-anniversary-iphone-size-options/">reported</a> in June that Apple had started ramping up work on two sizes of the 20th anniversary iPhone.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is also rumored to be developing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/09/23/20th-anniversary-iphone-brighter-oled/">thinner and brighter OLED panels</a> for the devices, along with under-display Face ID and potentially an under-display front-facing camera. However, Digital Chat Station says Apple is now testing a smaller Dynamic Island-style hole-punch design for the iPhone 20 Pro models that sounds similar to the new iPhone 18 Pro models, suggesting Apple may still be testing multiple approaches. <br/>
<br/>
Photo/video quality and concealment issues with the under-screen FaceTime camera on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> offer a timely example of the kind of challenge that Apple is likely facing in its quest to create an uninterrupted display design. Unless it can improve the implementation, a cutout for the front camera may be the compromise Apple has to make for the iPhone 20 Pro models.<br/>
